These recommendations are based on the power, versatility, and specifications of each router, focusing on factors that are typically important for wood routers: power (HP or RPM), versatility (variable speed, multiple bit compatibility), and ease of use. The Bosch MRF23EVS 2.3 HP Fixed-Base Router was ranked first due to its high power, trigger-controlled handle, and Constant Response circuitry. The Milwaukee M18 FUEL Compact Router ranked second due to its high RPM, POWERSTATE brushless motor, and cordless performance. The Makita RT0701C Compact Router ranked third due to its 1-1/4 HP, variable speed, and slim ergonomic body. The WEN 15-Amp Variable Speed Plunge Router ranked fourth for its versatility in offering 8,000–23,000 RPM, 1/4 and 1/2-inch bit compatibility, and included accessories. The RIDGID 1-1/2 HP Compact Router ranked fifth for its soft start, variable speed, and micro-adjust dial for precision depth control, as well as its compact size and lightweight design.

